Net-SNMP Linux package (x86_64)
===============================

Contents
--------
usr/local/       binaries (bin, sbin), libraries, headers, MIBs
install.sh       installer script
snmpd.conf       sample agent configuration
snmpd.service    systemd unit for snmpd

Requirements
------------
64-bit Linux with glibc and the OpenSSL runtime library:
  Debian/Ubuntu:  apt install libssl3
  RHEL/Fedora:    dnf install openssl-libs

Install
-------
  tar -xzf net-snmp-<version>-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
  cd net-snmp-<version>-linux-x86_64
  sudo ./install.sh              # copy to /usr/local and run ldconfig
  sudo ./install.sh --systemd    # same, plus install and start the snmpd service

install.sh copies sample snmpd.conf to /usr/local/etc/snmp/ only if no
snmpd.conf exists there. The default sample allows read-only access from
localhost with community "public"; edit it before exposing the agent.

Verify
------
  /usr/local/bin/snmpget -v2c -c public localhost sysDescr.0

If snmpd was not installed as a service, run it in the foreground with:
  sudo /usr/local/sbin/snmpd -f -Lo

Manual install without the script
---------------------------------
  sudo cp -a usr/local/. /usr/local/ && sudo ldconfig

Uninstall
---------
  sudo systemctl disable --now snmpd; sudo rm /etc/systemd/system/snmpd.service
  Remove the files listed by: tar -tzf net-snmp-<version>-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
  (paths under usr/local/), and /usr/local/etc/snmp if no longer needed.

Building the package
--------------------
On Linux or WSL (needs gcc, make, libssl-dev):
  bash installer/build-linux.sh
